            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use roots r, r + 1 and 1 − 2r with the cubic sum and product relationships.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let the roots be $r,r+1,s$. Using the sum of roots,\n$$\\begin{align*}r+(r+1)+s&=2\\\\s&=1-2r.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the product of roots,\n$$\\begin{align*}r(r+1)(1-2r)&=-18\\\\2r^3+r^2-r-18&=0\\\\(r-2)(2r^2+5r+9)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $2r^2+5r+9=0$, the discriminant is $25-72=-47<0$, so $r=2$. The roots are $2,3,-3$.\nUsing the sum of pairwise products,\n$$\\begin{align*}k&=(2)(3)+(2)(-3)+(3)(-3)\\\\k&=6-6-9\\\\k&=-9.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
